From 486625204658d9bc1348df350e5ccc3ebe6425eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: samuel oyedeji <oyedejisamuel05@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 04:07:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix: accept .ngrok-free.app, ack transcripts, widen
 silence window
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three fixes that together make a free-tier ngrok setup usable.

Accept `.ngrok-free.app` hosts, not just `.ngrok-free.dev`. ngrok issues both,
and the signature-validation bypass and WebSocket token fallback both keyed on
`.dev` only. On a `.app` tunnel Twilio's webhook is rejected with
`401 Invalid signature`, which the caller hears as "an application error has
occurred" and Twilio logs as an 11200.

Speak an acknowledgement as soon as a transcript lands. The transcript goes back
to the model as a tool result and the reply costs a full round-trip, so the
caller sits in dead air and concludes the call has broken — often hanging up,
which discards what they just said. This has to be server-side: an ack driven by
the model would arrive after the latency it exists to cover. Configurable via
`CALLME_ACK_MESSAGE`, empty to disable.

Raise the default silence window from 800ms to 1500ms. 800ms ends the turn
during an ordinary mid-sentence pause.

Also documents the tunables in .env.example and adds a README troubleshooting
section covering these symptoms plus ngrok's 3-tunnel limit and the Twilio trial
gate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
